<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<section xml:id="af-expanding">
  <title>Expanding Brackets</title>

  <objectives>
    <title>Learning Outcomes</title>
    <ul>
      <li><xref ref="lo-af-4" /> — Expand brackets</li>
      <li><xref ref="lo-af-5" /> — Expand binomials</li>
      <li><xref ref="lo-af-8" /> — Rearrange formulae</li>
    </ul>
  </objectives>

  <p>
    To expand a single bracket: multiply every term inside by the term outside.
    <me>a(b + c) = ab + ac</me>
  </p>
  <p>
    To expand two brackets (FOIL: First, Outer, Inner, Last):
    <me>(x + a)(x + b) = x^2 + bx + ax + ab = x^2 + (a+b)x + ab</me>
  </p>
  <p>
    Special cases worth memorising:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><m>(x + a)^2 = x^2 + 2ax + a^2</m></li>
    <li><m>(x - a)^2 = x^2 - 2ax + a^2</m></li>
    <li><m>(x + a)(x - a) = x^2 - a^2</m> (difference of two squares)</li>
  </ul>

  <exercises xml:id="exs-expanding">
    <title>Exercises</title>

    <exercise xml:id="ex-expand-single">
      <statement><p>Expand and simplify: <m>3(2x - 5) + 4(x + 1)</m></p></statement>
      <answer><p><m>10x - 11</m></p></answer>
      <solution><p><m>6x - 15 + 4x + 4 = 10x - 11</m></p></solution>
    </exercise>

    <exercise xml:id="ex-expand-binomials">
      <statement><p>Expand: <m>(x + 5)(x - 3)</m></p></statement>
      <answer><p><m>x^2 + 2x - 15</m></p></answer>
      <solution><p><m>x^2 - 3x + 5x - 15 = x^2 + 2x - 15</m></p></solution>
    </exercise>

  </exercises>

</section>
